{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"exegesis-stage","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1510,"label":"1 · Biblical Exegesis","color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"theology-stage","type":"group","x":600,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1510,"label":"2 · Theological Synthesis","color":"#9B72CF"},
		{"id":"formation-stage","type":"group","x":1200,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1510,"label":"3 · Formation Goals · working synthesis reviewed","color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"design-stage","type":"group","x":1800,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1510,"label":"4 · Session Design","color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"production-stage","type":"group","x":2400,"y":0,"width":1140,"height":1510,"label":"5 · Resource Production · drafts","color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"passage","type":"text","x":20,"y":50,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# Session 1 · Overview + 1:1–9\nFirst study gathering / G01A; introductions excluded.\n\n1:1–2 · Paul’s apostolic commission; resurrection; churches.\n1:3–5 · Grace, peace, Christ’s self-giving for sins and rescue; Father’s will; God’s glory.\n1:6–7 · Turning from the God who calls in grace.\n1:8–9 · The received gospel judges every messenger."},
		{"id":"overview","type":"text","x":20,"y":370,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# Book overview\nGentile inclusion, circumcision, table fellowship, promise/law, sonship, freedom, Spirit, cross, new creation.\n\nWorking map:\n• Chapters 1–2: received gospel and its defense.\n• Chapters 3–4: faith, promise, law, inheritance.\n• Chapters 5–6: freedom and Spirit-shaped life.\n\nAttend to the historical crisis without caricaturing Jewish identity or calling God’s law evil."},
		{"id":"source-record","type":"text","x":20,"y":730,"width":500,"height":480,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# Actual input and reading\nOriginal local input: `01 Research & Brainstorm/Galatians Study Session 1.canvas`.\n\nInput nodes: `source-status`, `exegesis`, `synthesis`, Keller notes `f6d3ec30e035955b`, questions `c7c3f5f322a011f8`.\n\nPaul’s current request sets 1:1–9. At his instruction, the Scripture quote is corrected to CSB. MSG is excluded from this session; its original input is retained as unused history.\n\nNo book edition/pages, Notion source link, or Traveling Light excerpt supplied. See synthesis for the verified reading link and source limits."},
		{"id":"gospel","type":"text","x":620,"y":50,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Central idea\nJesus gives himself to rescue sinners by grace; receive his gospel and test every proposed addition by it.\n\nCrucified and risen Christ → rescue received through faith → Spirit-shaped obedience.\n\nFaithful growth is fruit of grace rather than the price of acceptance. Historical explanation and contemporary applications remain distinct."},
		{"id":"keller","type":"text","x":620,"y":370,"width":500,"height":310,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Primary development resource\nKeller’s Galatians For You through Paul’s supplied quotations/notes and questions.\n\nBlock 1: apostolic witness; Jesus as rescuer; self-giving for sins and resurrection; grace humbles and gives hope.\nBlock 2: gospel revision as reversal; additions shift confidence; biblical gospel judges church and messenger.\n\nOriginal draft paraphrases and applications; no claim to full-book reading or verified pagination."},
		{"id":"boundaries","type":"text","x":620,"y":730,"width":500,"height":360,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Teaching boundaries\nPaul’s apostolic commission does not grant equivalent authority to present teachers through a private experience.\n\nVerses 8–9 invoke God’s judgment against a contrary gospel. Explain the warning seriously; do not use it against honest questions or every secondary disagreement.\n\nResponsibility, service, repentance, and spiritual disciplines are good; they cannot complete Christ’s saving work.\n\nPeterson remains secondary for freedom; integrate when actual material is available."},
		{"id":"mens-goals","type":"text","x":1220,"y":50,"width":500,"height":380,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Men · proposed\nReceive Christ’s rescue; move from self-reliance and a spiritual record toward honest gospel-shaped brotherhood.\n\nBelonging: needing help does not disqualify someone from welcome.\nBeholding: attend to the risen Jesus who gives himself for sinners.\nBecoming: name a self-justifying habit; take a step of repentance, prayer, and receiving help.\n\nExamples/practice: a spiritual scorecard; asking a brother for prayer/help."},
		{"id":"womens-goals","type":"text","x":1220,"y":490,"width":500,"height":380,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Women · proposed\nReceive Christ’s grace-given identity; move from comparison and approval toward truthful mutual encouragement.\n\nBelonging: appearance or a flawless faith story does not determine welcome.\nBeholding: attend to Christ’s sufficient work rather than comparative worth.\nBecoming: name an approval/comparison habit; take a step of gospel truth, prayer, and gracious encouragement.\n\nExamples/practice: comparing faith stories; listen before advice and encourage from Scripture."},
		{"id":"goals-review","type":"text","x":1220,"y":940,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Synthesis reviewed · October 13\nPaul reviewed this Canvas and called it “really good synthesis,” then requested separate participant handouts from it. Record synthesis review and production direction; full teaching scripts and actual exports have separate review scopes.\n\nThese are session pastoral angles rather than universal gender claims. Both pressures can affect anyone."},
		{"id":"flow","type":"text","x":1820,"y":50,"width":500,"height":340,"color":"#D6B34B","text":"# 6:30–8:00 PM · working flow\n6:30–6:50 · Community/check-in\n6:50–7:10 · Block 1: overview + 1:1–5; gospel as rescue\n7:10–7:20 · Table discussion 1\n7:20–7:40 · Block 2: 1:6–9; guard the gospel\n7:40–7:50 · Table discussion 2\n7:50–8:00 · Prayer/practice/announcements\n\nReading, observation, pauses, and transitions fit within teaching blocks. Rehearse before use; timing is planned, not measured."},
		{"id":"discussion-1","type":"text","x":1820,"y":450,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"#D96B6B","text":"# Discussion 1 · two core + reserve\nBase questions from supplied Keller bank:\n• Part 1 Q3: explain the gospel (core).\n• Part 1 Q1: heart/mind, encouragement/challenge (core).\n• Part 1 Q2: receiving apostolic authority (reserve).\n\nMen: grace and honest need.\nWomen: grace and comparative worth.\n\nDrafts record adaptation intent and leader cues. Ten minutes does not require all three questions."},
		{"id":"discussion-2","type":"text","x":1820,"y":810,"width":500,"height":370,"color":"#D96B6B","text":"# Discussion 2 · two core + reserve\n• Part 2 Q3: false-gospel dangers/additions (core).\n• Part 2 Q1: gospel truth in actual life (core).\n• Part 2 Q2: concern about distortion and its harm (reserve).\n\nMen: spiritual record/self-reliance and receiving help.\nWomen: approval/comparison and truthful encouragement.\n\nSource mentions three modern dangers without listing them. Do not invent Keller’s list; draft examples are original applications. Keep discussion anchored in the passage."},
		{"id":"production-status","type":"text","x":2420,"y":50,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"#9098A1","text":"# Approved participant handouts · v1.0\nSeparate three-page PDFs in phase 04; editable sources in phase 03. CSB 1:1–9; Part 1/2 labels; no MSG, timings, leader cues, or closing development note in handouts.\n\nWomen: October 27, 2026, after Paul moved Session 1 off October 13 that evening.\nMen: October 20, 2026.\n\nPaul approved the handout content October 13 with the two final edits applied. The October 27 PDF is the current women's edition. Full teaching-script review remains separate."},
		{"id":"mens-draft","type":"file","x":2420,"y":380,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Mens Galatians Session 1 Course Draft.md"},
		{"id":"womens-draft","type":"file","x":2420,"y":720,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Womens Galatians Session 1 Course Draft.md"},
		{"id":"synthesis-file","type":"file","x":2420,"y":1060,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/02 Structure & Synthesize/Collectives Galatians/Session 1 Synthesis.md"},
		{"id":"handoff","type":"text","x":0,"y":1620,"width":3540,"height":180,"color":"#9098A1","text":"# Final participant-resource handoff · October 13, 2026\nCanvas Organizer → Curriculum Editor → Resource Producer. Paul reviewed the synthesis, selected CSB, supplied dates, and approved the participant PDFs with two edits: change Block to Part and remove the closing development note. Current v1.0 exports are in phase 04; editable handout sources remain in phase 03. Full teaching-script review remains separate. No external distribution recorded."},
		{"id":"womens-pdf","type":"file","x":3020,"y":720,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/04 Design & Publish/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Womens Galatians G01A 2026-10-27 Handout.pdf"},
		{"id":"mens-pdf","type":"file","x":3020,"y":380,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/04 Design & Publish/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Mens Galatians G01A 2026-10-20 Handout.pdf"}
	],
